<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/add-10-dextrose-infusion> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Add 10% Dextrose Infusion" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "add-10-dextrose-infusion" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Once CBG improves to <14 mmol/L, 10% dextrose infusion should be added to act as the substrate for the insulin, to prevent hypoglycaemia." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Once CBG improves to <14 mmol/L, 10% dextrose infusion should be added to act as the substrate for the insulin, to prevent hypoglycaemia." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/administer-basal-insulin-alongside-friii> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Administer Basal Insulin Alongside FRIII" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "administer-basal-insulin-alongside-friii" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Basal insulin should always be administered alongside the FRIII. If the individual normally takes basal insulin (e.g. Lantus®, Degludec®, Levemir®, or human isophane insulin such as Insulatard® or Humalin S®) continue this at the usual dose and usual time. If the patient is not normally on basal insulin (i.e., new diagnosis or usually takes mixed insulin), please refer to medical team and local guideline to commence it alongside the FRIII as soon as possible." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Basal insulin should always be administered alongside the FRIII. If the individual normally takes basal insulin (e.g. Lantus®, Degludec®, Levemir®, or human isophane insulin such as Insulatard® or Humalin S®) continue this at the usual dose and usual time. If the patient is not normally on basal insulin (i.e., new diagnosis or usually takes mixed insulin), please refer to medical team and local guideline to commence it alongside the FRIII as soon as possible." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/administer-fluids-in-stages-for-dka> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Administer Fluids in Stages for DKA" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Individuals with DKA" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "administer-fluids-in-stages-for-dka" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "The table below outlines a typical fluid replacement regimen." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Fluid Volume 0.9% sodium chloride 1L * 1000ml over 1st hour 0.9% sodium chloride 1L with potassium chloride 1000ml over next 2 hours 0.9% sodium chloride 1L with potassium chloride 1000ml over next 2 hours 0.9% sodium chloride 1L with potassium chloride 1000ml over next 4 hours 0.9% sodium chloride 1L with potassium chloride 1000ml over next 4 hours 0.9% sodium chloride 1L with potassium chloride 1000ml over next 6 hours" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

