<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/guide-fluid-replacement-by-central-venous-pressure-in-high-risk-cases> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Guide Fluid Replacement by Central Venous Pressure in High-Risk Cases" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Individuals with DKA and high-risk comorbidities" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "guide-fluid-replacement-by-central-venous-pressure-in-high-risk-cases" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Fluids should be replaced cautiously, and if appropriate, guided by the central venous pressure measurements." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Fluids should be replaced cautiously, and if appropriate, guided by the central venous pressure measurements." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/hourly-point-of-care-glucose-and-ketone-testing> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Hourly Point of Care Glucose and Ketone Testing" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "hourly-point-of-care-glucose-and-ketone-testing" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Hourly point of care glucose (Lab if ‘HI’) and ketone testing" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Hourly point of care glucose (Lab if ‘HI’) and ketone testing" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/increase-insulin-infusion-rate-if-bicarbonate-not-rising> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Increase Insulin Infusion Rate if Bicarbonate Not Rising" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "increase-insulin-infusion-rate-if-bicarbonate-not-rising" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If blood ketone measurement is not available, use venous bicarbonate. If the bicarbonate is not rising by at least 3.0mmol/L/hr call a prescribing clinician to increase the insulin infusion rate by 1 unit/hr increments hourly until the bicarbonate is rising at this rate**" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If blood ketone measurement is not available, use venous bicarbonate. If the bicarbonate is not rising by at least 3.0mmol/L/hr call a prescribing clinician to increase the insulin infusion rate by 1 unit/hr increments hourly until the bicarbonate is rising at this rate**" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/increase-insulin-infusion-rate-if-glucose-not-falling> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Increase Insulin Infusion Rate if Glucose Not Falling" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "increase-insulin-infusion-rate-if-glucose-not-falling" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Alternatively use plasma glucose. If the glucose is not falling by at least 3.0mmol/L/hr call a prescribing clinician to increase the insulin infusion rate by 1.0 unit/hr increments hourly until glucose falls at this rate. Glucose level is not an accurate indicator of resolution of acidosis, so the acidosis resolution should be verified by venous gas analysis**" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Alternatively use plasma glucose. If the glucose is not falling by at least 3.0mmol/L/hr call a prescribing clinician to increase the insulin infusion rate by 1.0 unit/hr increments hourly until glucose falls at this rate. Glucose level is not an accurate indicator of resolution of acidosis, so the acidosis resolution should be verified by venous gas analysis**" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/increase-insulin-infusion-rate-if-ketones-not-falling> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Increase Insulin Infusion Rate if Ketones Not Falling" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "increase-insulin-infusion-rate-if-ketones-not-falling" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If blood ketone measurement is available and blood ketones are not falling by at least 0.5mmol/L/hr call a prescribing clinician to increase the insulin infusion rate by 1.0 unit/hr increments hourly until the ketones are falling at target rates (also check infusion**)" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If blood ketone measurement is available and blood ketones are not falling by at least 0.5mmol/L/hr call a prescribing clinician to increase the insulin infusion rate by 1.0 unit/hr increments hourly until the ketones are falling at target rates (also check infusion**)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/insulin-infusion-rate-at-0-05-unit-kg-hr> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Insulin Infusion Rate at 0.05 unit/kg/hr" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "insulin-infusion-rate-at-0-05-unit-kg-hr" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Once the glucose drops to <14mmol/L, in addition to adding a 10% dextrose infusion, the medical team may consider reducing the rate of intravenous insulin infusion to 0.05units/kg/hr to avoid the risk of developing hypoglycaemia and hypokalaemia." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Once the glucose drops to <14mmol/L, in addition to adding a 10% dextrose infusion, the medical team may consider reducing the rate of intravenous insulin infusion to 0.05units/kg/hr to avoid the risk of developing hypoglycaemia and hypokalaemia." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/insulin-infusion-rate-at-0-1-unit-kg-hr> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Insulin Infusion Rate at 0.1 unit/kg/hr" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "insulin-infusion-rate-at-0-1-unit-kg-hr" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "The rate of infusion is calculated using 0.1 unit/kg/hr." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The rate of infusion is calculated using 0.1 unit/kg/hr." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/manage-csii-in-dka-patients> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Manage CSII in DKA Patients" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients with DKA using CSII" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "manage-csii-in-dka-patients" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If the patient presents with DKA and using a continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion pump (CSII) then refer to local policy on management." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If the patient presents with DKA and using a continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion pump (CSII) then refer to local policy on management." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/management-of-diabetic-ketoacidosis-on-ward> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Management of Diabetic Ketoacidosis on Ward" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients with DKA" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "management-of-diabetic-ketoacidosis-on-ward" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Patients with DKA should only be managed on the ward if safe nursing to patient ratios are in place to ensure the timely requirements of DKA treatment are met." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Patients with DKA should only be managed on the ward if safe nursing to patient ratios are in place to ensure the timely requirements of DKA treatment are met." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/management-of-dka-in-ward-setting> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Management of DKA in Ward Setting" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "management-of-dka-in-ward-setting" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Some individuals can be safely managed in the ward, but others may need Level 2 (High Dependency Unit) care. Patients with DKA should only be managed on the ward if safe nursing to patient ratios are in place to ensure the timely requirements of DKA treatment are met. If this is not the case, patients with DKA will need Level 2 (High Dependency Unit) care." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Some individuals can be safely managed in the ward, but others may need Level 2 (High Dependency Unit) care. Patients with DKA should only be managed on the ward if safe nursing to patient ratios are in place to ensure the timely requirements of DKA treatment are met. If this is not the case , patients with DKA will need Level 2 (High Dependency Unit) care." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/monitor-blood-ketones-hourly> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Monitor Blood Ketones Hourly" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "monitor-blood-ketones-hourly" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Monitor blood ketones hourly using Trust approved meter until <0.6 mmol/L" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Monitor blood ketones hourly using Trust approved meter until <0.6 mmol/L" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/monitor-capillary-blood-glucose-hourly> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Monitor Capillary Blood Glucose Hourly" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "monitor-capillary-blood-glucose-hourly" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Monitor Capillary Blood Glucose hourly using Trust approved meter. If meter reads “over POCT QA range ie >27.8mmol/L\" or “Hi\", venous blood should be sent to the laboratory hourly or measured using venous blood in a blood gas analyser." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Monitor Capillary Blood Glucose hourly using Trust approved meter. If meter reads “over POCT QA range ie >27.8mmol/L\" or “Hi\", venous blood should be sent to the laboratory hourly or measured using venous blood in a blood gas analyser." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/overlap-between-insulin-infusion-and-first-rapid-acting-mixed-insulin> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Overlap Between Insulin Infusion and First Rapid-Acting/Mixed Insulin" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "overlap-between-insulin-infusion-and-first-rapid-acting-mixed-insulin" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Eating: There should be an overlap between the insulin infusion and first administration of rapid acting/ mixed insulin (preferably via the patients usual method i.e. injection or insulin pump)" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "There should be an overlap between the insulin infusion and first administration of rapid acting/ mixed insulin (preferably via the patients usual method i.e. injection or insulin pump)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/overlap-between-insulin-infusion-and-rapid-acting-insulin> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Overlap Between Insulin Infusion and Rapid Acting Insulin" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients transitioning from IV insulin infusion to subcutaneous rapid acting insulin" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "overlap-between-insulin-infusion-and-rapid-acting-insulin" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "There should be an overlap between the insulin infusion and first injection of rapid acting insulin (e.g. Novorapid®, Trurapi®, Humalog®, Apidra®, FiAsp®). The rapid acting insulin should be injected with the meal and the intravenous insulin and fluids discontinued 30 to 60 minutes later" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "There should be an overlap between the insulin infusion and first injection of rapid acting insulin (e.g. Novorapid®, Trurapi®, Humalog®, Apidra®, FiAsp®). The rapid acting insulin should be injected with the meal and the intravenous insulin and fluids discontinued 30 to 60 minutes later" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/potassium-replacement-based-on-serum-level> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Potassium Replacement Based on Serum Level" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "potassium-replacement-based-on-serum-level" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Potassium level in first 24 hours (mmol/L) Potassium replacement in mmol/L of infusion solution Over 5.5 Nil 3.5-5.5 40 Below 3.5 Senior review as additional potassium needs to be given" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Potassium level in first 24 hours (mmol/L) Potassium replacement in mmol/L of infusion solution Over 5.5 Nil 3.5-5.5 40 Below 3.5 Senior review as additional potassium needs to be given" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/prepare-insulin-infusion-with-human-soluble-insulin-in-0-9-sodium-chloride> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Prepare Insulin Infusion with Human Soluble Insulin in 0.9% Sodium Chloride" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Individuals with DKA" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "prepare-insulin-infusion-with-human-soluble-insulin-in-0-9-sodium-chloride" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "This is made of 50 units of human soluble insulin (Actrapid®, Humulin S®) made up to 50ml with 0.9% sodium chloride solution." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "This is made of 50 units of human soluble insulin (Actrapid®, Humulin S®) made up to 50ml with 0.9% sodium chloride solution." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/prescribe-and-date-intravenous-insulin-and-fluid-management-protocols> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Prescribe and Date Intravenous Insulin and Fluid Management Protocols" ;
