<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/reintroducing-subcutaneous-insulin-after-fixed-mix-insulin> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Reintroducing Subcutaneous Insulin After Fixed-Mix Insulin" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients previously on twice daily fixed-mix insulin (e.g., Novomix 30®, Humalog Mix 50®, Humalin M3®)" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "reintroducing-subcutaneous-insulin-after-fixed-mix-insulin" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Re-introduce the subcutaneous insulin before breakfast or before the evening meal. Do not change at any other time. Maintain the insulin infusion for 30 to 60 minutes after the subcutaneous insulin was given" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Re-introduce the subcutaneous insulin before breakfast or before the evening meal. Do not change at any other time. Maintain the insulin infusion for 30 to 60 minutes after the subcutaneous insulin was given" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/remove-csii-and-replace-with-subcutaneous-basal-insulin-if-no-local-policy> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Remove CSII and Replace with Subcutaneous Basal Insulin if No Local Policy" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients with DKA using CSII and no local policy" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "remove-csii-and-replace-with-subcutaneous-basal-insulin-if-no-local-policy" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If no local policy exists, escalate to the Drs, explain to the individual patient that their CSII needs to be removed and stored safely and replaced with subcutaneous basal insulin which the Drs should prescribe in line with local policy." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If no local policy exists, escalate to the Drs, explain to the individual patient that their CSII needs to be removed and stored safely and replaced with subcutaneous basal insulin which the Drs should prescribe in line with local policy." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/resolution-of-dka-defined-by-ketones-and-ph> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Resolution of DKA Defined by Ketones and pH" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "resolution-of-dka-defined-by-ketones-and-ph" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Diagnosis" ;
    dmo:statement "Resolution of DKA is defined as ketones less than 0.6mmol/L, and venous pH over 7.3" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Resolution of DKA is defined as ketones less than 0.6mmol/L, and venous pH over 7.3" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/restarting-short-acting-insulin-after-basal-insulin> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Restarting Short Acting Insulin After Basal Insulin" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Patients previously on once or twice daily basal insulin" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "restarting-short-acting-insulin-after-basal-insulin" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If the person was previously on a basal insulin once or twice a day (e.g., Lantus®, Semglee®, Abasaglar®, Degludec®, Levemir®, or human isophane insulin such as Insulatard® or Humalin I®) this should have been continued and thus the only action should be to restart their normal short acting insulin at the next meal" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If the person was previously on a basal insulin once or twice a day (e.g., Lantus®, Semglee®, Abasaglar®, Degludec®, Levemir®, or human isophane insulin such as Insulatard® or Humalin I®) this should have been continued and thus the only action should be to restart their normal short acting insulin at the next meal" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/review-by-consultant-physician-for-severe-dka-signs> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Review by Consultant Physician for Severe DKA Signs" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Individuals with DKA exhibiting severe signs" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "review-by-consultant-physician-for-severe-dka-signs" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Referral" ;
    dmo:statement "If the individual exhibits any of these signs they should be reviewed by a consultant physician and considered for referral to a Level 2/HDU (High Dependency Unit) environment." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If the individual exhibits any of these signs they should be reviewed by a consultant physician and considered for referral to a Level 2/HDU (High Dependency Unit) environment." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_02_nursing_management_for_dka_v1_20122022> .

