    dmo:evidenceQuote "Stopping intravenous insulin infusion: eating and drinking reliably If they were on basal bolus insulin • If the person was previously on a basal insulin once or twice a day (e.g., Lantus®, Semglee®, Abasaglar®, Degludec®, Levemir®, or human isophane insulin such as Insulatard® or Humalin I®) this should have been continued and thus the only action should be to restart their normal short acting insulin at th" ;
